From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:03:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell: Set SPCAPCTRL with the IGD too

Document 492662 sets SPCAPCTRL (bit 25 of ARCHDIS) in the remapping
engine for the devices other than the IGD only when the IGD is absent.
With the IGD present it stays clear, and that engine reports 2 MiB and
1 GiB pages (Linux: "dmar1: ... cap d2008c20660462") but does not take
them: Linux with DMA translation maps 2 MiB pages and gets faults with
reason 0x0c, "non-zero reserved fields in PTE", on 2 MiB-aligned
addresses and the 4 KiB pages after them, and the transfers are lost.

On a ThinkPad W541 with Linux 7.2.9 and intel_iommu=on, 32 GiB of 4 MiB
O_DIRECT reads into transparent huge pages, together with every file in
/usr read through the page cache, gave 21 such faults from the SATA
controller, the first ones already during boot, and btrfs found blocks
of zeros. With SPCAPCTRL set, the same test gives none. The capability
register reads the same in both cases.

The vendor firmware of Haswell machines does not run into this: in the
Linux logs of linux-hardware.org, about 1200 logs of Lenovo, Dell, HP
and Apple Haswell laptops and desktops report no superpages for this
engine ("cap d2008020660462"). Where the superpages are reported, the
same faults show up: a MacBookPro11,5 (from its GPU and its SSD) and Z97
boards, where intel_iommu=sp_off made them go away.

Set SPCAPCTRL whether the IGD is there or not.

TEST=On a ThinkPad W541, ARCHDIS of the engine reads 0x820a5003 and the
test above gives no DMAR faults with Linux 7.2.9 and intel_iommu=on.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
index f58a7b04f..779ff23c5 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
@@ -174,10 +174,15 @@ static void northbridge_setup_iommu(void)
 
 		clrsetbits32p(VTVC0_BASE_ADDRESS + 0xf04, 0xf << 15, 1 << 15);
 
-		u32 vtvc0_archdis = 0x000a5003 | DMAR_LCKDN;
-		if (pci_read_config16(PCI_DEV(0, 2, 0), PCI_DEVICE_ID) == 0xffff) {
-			vtvc0_archdis |= SPCAPCTRL;
-		}
+		/*
+		 * The document sets SPCAPCTRL only without the IGD. Without it
+		 * this engine reports 2 MiB and 1 GiB pages but rejects them:
+		 * Linux gets DMA faults "non-zero reserved fields in PTE" on
+		 * the 2 MiB pages it maps, and the transfers are lost. With it
+		 * set they work. The capability register is the same either
+		 * way.
+		 */
+		const u32 vtvc0_archdis = 0x000a5003 | SPCAPCTRL | DMAR_LCKDN;
 		write32p(VTVC0_BASE_ADDRESS + ARCHDIS, vtvc0_archdis);
 	}
 	if (cpu_is_broadwell()) {
-- 
